The denominator requires $x\ne2$. Both sides are positive, so reciprocating reverses the inequality:
$|x-2|\ge4$.
$\begin{aligned}x-2&\le-4\\x&\le-2\end{aligned}$
or
$\begin{aligned}x-2&\ge4\\x&\ge6\end{aligned}$
The solution is $(-\infty,-2]\cup[6,\infty)$. It already excludes $x=2$.
